{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>You shall not wear sha'atnez.</b> Because the parokhet was made of six — six threads of linen and of techelet and techelet wool — behold, wool and linen together, and the Holy One, blessed be He, did not want His sons to make a replica of it, just as we find regarding the incense: ״איש אשר יעשה כמוה להריח בה״ etc., and likewise the Sages said: a person should not make a house in the form of the Heikhal, a portico in the form of the Ulam, etc. Another explanation: because Cain offered flax seed and Abel brought from the firstborn of his flock, which is a type of wool — the Holy One, blessed be He, did not want them to be joined together, because over those they became divided."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {0 "The parokhet description reads 'six — six threads'; the repetition is translated as it stands. The Aramaic terms כיתנא (linen), עמרא (wool), and תכל׳ (abbreviated techelet) are resolved silently."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:01:18.090560538Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}